/target

# `tests/cross` is a crate of its own, outside the workspace, that
# `tests/cross_targets.rs` compiles for other machines; Cargo writes its lock
# file the first time the test runs. Its artifacts go to `target/cross-check`.
/tests/cross/Cargo.lock

# `tests/rust-analyzer-fixture` is the same arrangement for
# `scripts/check-rust-analyzer.sh`: a crate outside the workspace, whose lock
# file appears the first time rust-analyzer loads it. Its artifacts go to
# `target/rust-analyzer-fixture`.
/tests/rust-analyzer-fixture/Cargo.lock

# insta writes these next to the blessed snapshots when one fails
*.snap.new
*.pending-snap

# The conformance corpora `scripts/fetch-testsuites.sh` fetches. GCC and LLVM
# are far too large to vendor and too large to be submodules of a small crate,
# so each is a blobless, sparse checkout of one directory, pinned in the
# script. (c-testsuite *is* a submodule, and stays checked in as one.)
/third_party/gcc
/third_party/llvm-project
